{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-1-timothy-001",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 1,
  "title": "1 Timothy 1",
  "display_title": "1 Timothy 1",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "1-timothy",
  "book": "1 Timothy",
  "bookName": "1 Timothy",
  "bookOrder": 54,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 1,
  "sortOrder": 54001,
  "verseCount": 20,
  "aliases": [
    "1 Tim",
    "1Tim",
    "1 Ti",
    "1Ti"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ by the commandment of God our Saviour, and Lord Jesus Christ, which is our hope;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Unto Timothy, my own son in the faith: Grace, mercy, and peace, from God our Father and Jesus Christ our Lord.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "As I besought thee to abide still at Ephesus, when I went into Macedonia, that thou mightest charge some that they teach no other doctrine,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Neither give heed to fables and endless genealogies, which minister questions, rather than godly edifying which is in faith: so do.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Now the end of the commandment is charity out of a pure heart, and of a good conscience, and of faith unfeigned:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "From which some having swerved have turned aside unto vain jangling;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Desiring to be teachers of the law; understanding neither what they say, nor whereof they affirm.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "But we know that the law is good, if a man use it lawfully;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Knowing this, that the law is not made for a righteous man, but for the lawless and disobedient, for the ungodly and for sinners, for unholy and profane, for murderers of fathers and murderers of mothers, for manslayers,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "For whoremongers, for them that defile themselves with mankind, for menstealers, for liars, for perjured persons, and if there be any other thing that is contrary to sound doctrine;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "According to the glorious gospel of the blessed God, which was committed to my trust.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "And I thank Christ Jesus our Lord, who hath enabled me, for that he counted me faithful, putting me into the ministry;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Who was before a blasphemer, and a persecutor, and injurious: but I obtained mercy, because I did it ignorantly in unbelief.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "And the grace of our Lord was exceeding abundant with faith and love which is in Christ Jesus.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "This is a faithful saying, and worthy of all acceptation, that Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners; of whom I am chief.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Howbeit for this cause I obtained mercy, that in me first Jesus Christ might shew forth all longsuffering, for a pattern to them which should hereafter believe on him to life everlasting.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Now unto the King eternal, immortal, invisible, the only wise God, be honour and glory for ever and ever. Amen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "This charge I commit unto thee, son Timothy, according to the prophecies which went before on thee, that thou by them mightest war a good warfare;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Holding faith, and a good conscience; which some having put away concerning faith have made shipwreck:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:1:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Of whom is Hymenaeus and Alexander; whom I have delivered unto Satan, that they may learn not to blaspheme.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 1:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:1:20"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
